        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: update dependencies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's workspace dependency set had accumulated routine version drift, while several newest releases changed APIs, peers, platform support, or Node engine ranges. Updating only the lockfile would leave publishable shrinkwraps and integration contracts stale.\n\nCloses #99952.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Refresh direct dependencies across the root package, packages, UI, and plugins.\n- Regenerate the pnpm lockfile and publishable npm shrinkwraps.\n- Adapt the affected ACP, grammY, Pierre diffs, Codex, Copilot, and Node type contracts.\n- Remove the obsolete Claude ACP patch and no-longer-direct Pierre theme dependency.\n- Keep `@openclaw/fs-safe` 0.4.1's current pinned-write protections while making only `fsync` `EPERM` best-effort, matching the existing media-store contract.\n- Suppress reconnect-drain log amplification when startup recovery or a live send already owns a delivery claim; hosted QA exposed more than 100,000 duplicate diagnostics from one pending entry.\n- Keep explicit holds where the newest release conflicts with OpenClaw's supported Node, peer, or platform matrix.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers receive current compatible dependency releases without changing OpenClaw configuration or public APIs. Codex model metadata, Telegram bot metadata, ACP completion handling, diffs rendering, secure media writes, and reconnect recovery remain aligned with their upstream and product contracts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Replacement exact-SHA release gate: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28713529171 — passed cleanly for `f158c4d7f3087cddd04f5c78744fb4637dcf6478`.\n- Dependency Guard passed on Actions run `28709745284`.\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox type/package-boundary proof: `tbx_01kwpjxnkqw46pzf91982rj81v` / Actions run `28706788460`.\n- Blacksmith Testbox-through-Crabbox targeted QA proof: `tbx_01kwpmhnjdntp0haasdfr6pwxk` / Actions run `28707489550` (`native-command-session-target`, 1/1 passed).\n- Focused recovery + Telegram proof: 89/89 tests passed.\n- Media-store proof: 47/47 tests passed against patched `@openclaw/fs-safe` 0.4.1.\n- Browser/Undici proof: 59/59 tests passed.\n- Frozen install, build, package patch guard, shrinkwrap guard, supply-chain policy, vulnerability gate, and formatting checks passed.\n- Direct Codex source inspection plus live harness `model/list` proof confirmed CLI/config and model metadata contracts.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview completed with no accepted/actionable findings after the final reconnect-drain regression fix.\n\nIntentional latest-version holds: Apache Arrow for LanceDB's peer range; `audio-decode` for Baileys' peer range; jscpd for supported runner binaries; `oxlint-tsgolint` for the current lint contract; sigstore and tsdown for supported Node ranges; deprecated `@zed-industries/codex-acp` pending migration to its incompatible replacement CLI.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
